      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "eeb61297-7631-5457-80bb-3dfc3aff9b84",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peter Desaga, Michael Faraday, Robert Wilhelm Bunsen, Georg Lunge, Ferdinand Cohn\n- Organizations: University of Heidelberg, University of Breslau\n- Products: Bunsen burner, laboratory burner\n- Topics: instrument making, electromagnetism, electrochemistry\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Faraday was an English scientist who lived from 22 September 1791 to 25 August 1867 and contributed to electromagnetism and electrochemistry.\n- In 1855, Peter Desaga perfected Michael Faraday’s earlier laboratory burner design into the Bunsen burner.\n- Peter Desaga was a German instrument maker at the University of Heidelberg who worked with Robert Wilhelm Bunsen.\n- Robert Wilhelm Bunsen and his laboratory assistant Peter Desaga developed the Bunsen burner as an improvement on laboratory burners then in use.\n- Georg Lunge studied at Heidelberg under Robert Bunsen and at the University of Breslau, where he graduated in 1859 for work with Ferdinand Cohn.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
