        "text": "Page: Peter Desaga. Sentence: Peter Desaga was a German instrument maker at the University of Heidelberg who worked with Robert Wilhelm Bunsen.\nPage: Peter Desaga. Sentence: In 1855, Desaga perfected an earlier design of the laboratory burner by Michael Faraday into the Bunsen burner.\nPage: Michael Faraday. Sentence: Michael Faraday FRS ( ; 22 September 1791 – 25 August 1867) was an English scientist who contributed to the study of electromagnetism and electrochemistry.\nPage: Robert Bunsen. Sentence: With his laboratory assistant, Peter Desaga, he developed the Bunsen burner, an improvement on the laboratory burners then in use.\nPage: Georg Lunge. Sentence: He studied at Heidelberg (under Robert Bunsen) and Breslau, graduating at the latter university in 1859, for the work with Ferdinand Cohn.",
